You are supporting a process mining research prototype.
Use only the synthetic scenario information provided below.
Do not invent company-specific system names, product names, confidential logs, internal metrics, or real organizational details.
Return valid JSON only. Do not wrap it in Markdown.

Scenario ID: S03
Scenario title: Wafer Sample Transfer and Disposal Request
Initial workflow description:
Samples are moved when they are needed for evaluation. After evaluation, unnecessary samples are checked and disposed of through a request process.

Clarification questions:
[
  {
    "id": "Q1",
    "question": "Who is responsible for initiating a sample transfer request — is it the engineer requesting the evaluation, a dedicated lab technician, or is the transfer triggered automatically by a system event?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q2",
    "question": "What specific criteria or conditions determine that a sample is 'unnecessary' after evaluation and should be flagged for disposal — for example, are there defined evaluation outcomes, age thresholds, or quantity rules?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q3",
    "question": "Does the disposal request require approval from any person or role before it can be executed, and if so, what is the approval authority and what conditions might lead to a rejection?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q4",
    "question": "What system or tool is currently used to track sample status, location, and evaluation results throughout this workflow — for example, a laboratory information management system, a spreadsheet, or another platform?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q5",
    "question": "What is the expected output at the end of the disposal request process — for example, is a disposal record, confirmation log, or compliance certificate generated, and where is it stored?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q6",
    "question": "Approximately how many sample transfers and disposal requests occur per week or month, and are they handled individually on demand or grouped into scheduled batches?"
  }
]
Reference workflow for oracle use:
{
  "goal": "Move required wafer samples for evaluation and dispose of completed samples through traceable approval.",
  "actors": [
    "sample requester",
    "sample manager",
    "verification engineer",
    "approver"
  ],
  "systems": [
    "sample tracking sheet",
    "transfer request form",
    "approval system",
    "storage location registry"
  ],
  "inputs": [
    "sample identifier",
    "evaluation purpose",
    "target location",
    "disposal reason"
  ],
  "outputs": [
    "transfer approval",
    "updated sample status",
    "disposal record",
    "physical confirmation note"
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "id": "A1",
      "name": "Identify required sample and evaluation purpose",
      "actor": "sample requester"
    },
    {
      "id": "A2",
      "name": "Submit sample transfer request",
      "actor": "sample requester"
    },
    {
      "id": "A3",
      "name": "Approve transfer request",
      "actor": "approver"
    },
    {
      "id": "A4",
      "name": "Physically confirm sample",
      "actor": "sample manager"
    },
    {
      "id": "A5",
      "name": "Move sample to target location",
      "actor": "sample manager"
    },
    {
      "id": "A6",
      "name": "Update sample status after evaluation",
      "actor": "verification engineer"
    },
    {
      "id": "A7",
      "name": "Submit disposal request for completed sample",
      "actor": "verification engineer"
    },
    {
      "id": "A8",
      "name": "Approve and record disposal",
      "actor": "approver"
    }
  ],
  "decisions": [
    {
      "id": "D1",
      "condition": "Is the sample available and correctly identified?",
      "branches": [
        "available",
        "not found or mismatched"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "D2",
      "condition": "Is disposal allowed after evaluation?",
      "branches": [
        "allowed",
        "retain sample"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "exceptions": [
    "sample identifier mismatch",
    "missing physical sample",
    "approval delay",
    "retention requirement"
  ],
  "dependencies": [
    {
      "from": "A1",
      "to": "A2",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A2",
      "to": "A3",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A3",
      "to": "A4",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A4",
      "to": "A5",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A5",
      "to": "A6",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A6",
      "to": "A7",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A7",
      "to": "A8",
      "type": "control_flow"
    }
  ],
  "automation_opportunities": [
    {
      "target": "A2",
      "rationale": "Transfer request fields can be pre-filled from sample identifiers and evaluation purpose."
    },
    {
      "target": "A6",
      "rationale": "Status updates can be prompted automatically after scheduled evaluation completion."
    },
    {
      "target": "A7",
      "rationale": "Disposal candidates can be suggested when retention conditions are not met."
    }
  ]
}
Task: Simulate a concise domain expert who answers only these questions using the reference workflow.
Do not reveal the full reference workflow. Do not add details not needed by the questions.
If a requested fact is absent, explicitly say it is not specified; do not guess.
Use at most 80 words per answer. Return one answer for each question, with matching ID and question text.
Return JSON: {"answers": [{"question_id": "Q1", "question": "original question", "answer": "grounded answer"}]}
